      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-90694",
      ":question/problem": "Since $2005$, the population of a certain town grows at a rate $r(t)$ given by the function \n \n\n$$\nr(t)=200{e}^{0.2t}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in people per year, and $t>0$ is the time in years since $2005.$\n\nTo the nearest integer, by how many people did the population of the town increase between the years $2010$ and $2015?$"
